1. e4 e5 2. f4 {... etc. "A King's Gambit Decline in which Mr. Weisberg obtained the better position, but on his 9th move he played weakly by putting his knight completely out of play and followed this up by losing time in capturing a pawn with his queen. The result was that his position on the 14th move had become very inferior; his king was driven into the open, he lost several pawns, and finally a rook by an oversight, upon which he resigned." Source: The Field, 28 March 1914.} 0-1

