1. d4 {... etc. "Another Queen's Pawn Opening carefully played by both sides and without any marked feature until finally White commenced an attack by advancing his pawns on the King's side. At first the attack looked promising, but one or two inferior moves compromised his position and when time was called, he was two pawns down. The game was adjudicated by Mr. Burn as a win for Oxford." Source: The Field, 28 March 1914} 0-1

